.Dd June 26, 2026
.Dt CAP_MMAP_CAPMODE 2
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cap_mmap_capmode
.Nd require capability mode for mmap on a descriptor
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libc
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/capsicum.h
.Ft int
.Fn cap_mmap_capmode "int fd"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn cap_mmap_capmode
system call sets a monotonic per-descriptor flag that requires the
calling process to be in capability mode
.Pq see Xr cap_enter 2
before the descriptor may be mapped into memory with
.Xr mmap 2 .
.Pp
Once set, any attempt to
.Xr mmap 2
the descriptor from a process not in capability mode will fail with
.Er ENOTCAPABLE .
.Pp
The flag is monotonic: once set it cannot be cleared.
Calling
.Fn cap_mmap_capmode
on a descriptor that already has the flag set is permitted and has no
effect.
.Pp
This is typically used on shared memory descriptors created with
.Xr shm_open 2
that should only be accessible to sandboxed processes.
.Pp
This system call is allowed in capability mode
.Pq see Xr cap_enter 2 .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Rv -std
.Sh ERRORS
.Fn cap_mmap_capmode
succeeds unless:
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EBADF
The
.Fa fd
argument is not a valid active descriptor.
.It Bq Er ENOSYS
The running kernel was compiled without
.Cd "options CAPABILITIES" .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cap_enter 2 ,
.Xr mmap 2 ,
.Xr shm_open 2 ,
.Xr capsicum 4
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn cap_mmap_capmode
system call first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
